 "why": {
  "this regulation shall enter into force on the day following that of its publication in the official journal of the european union": "말뭉치에서 \"게재된 날의 다음 날\"이 우세하고 원문(the day following that of)에도 더 가깝다.",
  "except: 3105 60 00 - mineral or chemical fertilisers containing the two fertilising elements phosphorus and potassium": "말뭉치에서 우세한 \"비료 요소\"를 쓰고 법령 문체의 \"또는\"을 쓴 변형이다.",
  "article 5 is amended as follows": "개정 지시문은 \"제○조를 다음과 같이 개정한다\"가 말뭉치에서 우세하고 능동 법령 문체에 맞다.",
  "article 21 is amended as follows": "개정 지시문은 \"제○조를 다음과 같이 개정한다\"가 말뭉치에서 우세한 형식이다.",
  "article 23 is amended as follows": "개정 지시문은 \"제○조를 다음과 같이 개정한다\"가 말뭉치에서 우세한 형식이다.",
  "article 26 is amended as follows": "개정 지시문은 \"제○조를 다음과 같이 개정한다\"가 말뭉치에서 우세한 형식이다.",
  "the measures provided for in this regulation are in accordance with the opinion of the cbam committee": "\"의견에 부합한다\"가 말뭉치에서 우세하고 국문 문장 종결로 자연스럽다.",
  "'emission source' means a separately identifiable part of an installation or a process within an installation, from which relevant greenhouse gases are emitted": "쉼표로 \"관련 온실가스가 배출되는\"이 두 대상을 모두 수식함을 분명히 한다.",
  "'uncertainty' means a parameter, associated with the result of the determination of a quantity, that characterises the dispersion of the values that could reasonably be attributed to the particular quantity, including the effects of systematic as well as of random factors, expressed in per cent, and describes a confidence interval around the mean value comprising 95 % of inferred values taking into account any asymmetry of the distribution of values": "\"a quantity\"를 \"어떤 양\"으로 옮겨 원문에 더 충실하다.",
  "'combustion emissions' means greenhouse gas emissions occurring during the exothermic reaction of a fuel with oxygen": "\"exothermic reaction of a fuel with oxygen\"의 명사 구조를 그대로 살렸다.",
  "'emission factor' means the average emission rate of a greenhouse gas relative to the activity data of a source stream assuming complete oxidation for combustion and complete conversion for all other chemical reactions": "두 변형 모두 정확하며 \"~의 경우\"가 더 간결한 법령 문체다.",
  "'conversion factor' means the ratio of carbon emitted as co2 to the total carbon contained in the source stream before the emitting process takes place, expressed as a fraction, considering co emitted to the atmosphere as the molar equivalent amount of co2": "원문 어순을 따르는 정의 구조이고 \"분수로 표시한\"이 다른 정의(바이오매스 비율)와 일관된다.",
  "'accuracy' means the closeness of the agreement between the result of a measurement and the true value of the particular quantity or a reference value determined empirically using internationally accepted and traceable calibration materials and standard methods, taking into account both random and systematic factors": "\"일치 정도\"가 \"일치의 근접성\"보다 자연스러운 계량 용어다.",
  "'calibration' means the set of operations, which establishes, under specified conditions, the relations between values indicated by a measuring instrument or measuring system, or values represented by a material measure or a reference material and the corresponding values of a quantity realised by a reference standard": "reference material의 표준 계량 용어인 \"표준물질\"이 말뭉치에서도 우세하다.",
  "'conservative' means that a set of assumptions is defined in order to ensure that no under-estimation of reported emissions or over-estimation of production of heat, electricity or goods occurs": "말뭉치에서 \"과소평가/과대평가\"가 우세하다.",
  "'waste' means any substance or object which the holder discards or intends or is required to discard, excluding substances that have been intentionally modified or contaminated in order to meet this definition": "법령 문체의 \"또는\"을 쓴 법령 변형이다.",
  "'data flow activities' mean activities related to the acquisition, processing and handling of data that are needed to draft an emissions report from primary source data": "primary data 용어집 표기(1차 데이터)와 일관된 \"1차 출처 데이터\"를 쓴다.",
  "'net calorific value' (ncv) means the specific amount of energy released as heat when a fuel or material undergoes complete combustion with oxygen under standard conditions, less the heat of vaporisation of any water formed": "\"any water\"의 \"모든\"을 빠뜨리지 않아 원문에 더 충실하다.",
  "'process emissions' means greenhouse gas emissions other than combustion emissions occurring as a result of intentional and unintentional reactions between substances or their transformation, for a primary purpose other than the generation of heat, including from the following processes": "원문 구조(연소배출 외의 온실가스 배출로서)를 따라 정의가 더 명확하다.",
  "'batch' means an amount of fuel or material representatively sampled and characterised, and transferred as one shipment or continuously over a specific period of time": "피동 구조가 일관되어 \"시료채취되고 특성이 분석되어 이송되는 양\"의 관계가 정확하다.",
  "'mixed material' means a material which contains both biomass and fossil carbon": "두 변형 모두 정확하며 contains를 \"포함하는\"으로 옮긴 2025 법령 변형을 택한다.",
  "'preliminary emission factor' means the assumed total emission factor of a fuel or material based on the carbon content of its biomass fraction and its fossil fraction before multiplying it by the fossil fraction to produce the emission factor": "용어집 표기 \"바이오매스 비율\"과 \"화석 비율\"을 쓴다.",
  "'biomass fraction' means the ratio of carbon stemming from biomass to the total carbon content of a fuel or material, expressed as a fraction": "\"분수로 표시한\"이 전환계수 정의 등과 일관된다.",
  "'continuous emission measurement' means a set of operations having the objective of determining the value of a quantity by means of periodic measurements, applying either measurements in the stack or extractive procedures with a measuring instrument located close to the stack, whilst excluding measurement methodologies based on the collection of individual samples from the stack": "두 변형의 차이가 미미하여 규칙 선택을 유지한다.",
  "'fossil carbon' means inorganic and organic carbon that is not biomass": "법령 문체의 \"및\"을 쓴다.",
  "'measurement point' means the emission source for which continuous emission measurement systems (cems) are used for emission measurement, or the cross-section of a pipeline system for which the co2 flow is determined using continuous measurement systems": "emission measurement를 \"배출량 측정\"으로 옮겨 말뭉치 용어(배출량)와 일관된다.",
  "'fugitive emissions' means irregular or unintended emissions from sources that are not localised, or too diverse or too small to be monitored individually": "원문 구조(국지화되지 않았거나, 개별 모니터링하기에 너무 다양하거나 작은)를 정확히 따른다.",
  "'standard conditions' means temperature of 273,15 k and pressure conditions of 101 325 pa defining normal cubic metres (nm3)": "말뭉치에서 \"표준 세제곱미터\"가 우세하다.",
  "'measurable heat' means a net heat flow transported through identifiable pipelines or ducts using a heat transfer medium, such as, in particular, steam, hot air, water, oil, liquid metals and salts, for which a heat meter is or could be installed": "\"순열 흐름\"(permutation으로 읽힘)이 아닌 \"순 열 흐름\"이고 \"열매체\"가 표준 용어다.",
  "'data set' means one type of data, either at installation level or production process level as relevant in the circumstances, as any of the following": "법령 문체의 \"또는\"을 쓴다.",
  "emissions data over a full reporting period shall be expressed in tonnes co2e rounded to full tonnes": "말뭉치에서 \"CO2e 톤으로\" 표기가 우세하다.",
  "all parameters used to calculate the emissions shall be rounded to include all significant digits for the purpose of calculating and reporting emissions": "두 변형 모두 정확하며 차이가 미미하여 2025 법령 변형을 택한다.",
  "specific direct and indirect embedded emissions shall be expressed in tonnes of co2e per tonne of goods, rounded to include all significant digits, with a maximum of 5 digits after the comma": "말뭉치에서 \"CO2e 톤으로\" 표기가 우세하고 제59군 선택과 일관된다.",
  "direct emissions at installation level include combustion and process emissions": "\"include\"를 능동 \"포함한다\"로 옮긴 간결한 법령 문체다.",
  "accuracy: the chosen monitoring methodology shall ensure that emission determination is neither systematically nor knowingly inaccurate. any source of inaccuracies shall be identififed and reduced as far as possible. due diligence shall be exercised to ensure that the calculation and measurement of emissions exhibit the highest achievable accuracy": "systematically inaccurate는 계측 용어 \"계통적\"이 맞고 말뭉치에서도 우세하다.",
  "integrity of methodology: the chosen monitoring methodology shall enable reasonable assurance of the integrity of emission data to be reported. emissions shall be determined using the appropriate monitoring methodologies set out in this annex. reported emission data shall be free from material misstatement, avoid bias in the selection and presentation of information, and provide a credible and balanced account of the embedded emissions of installation's produced goods": "integrity는 확정된 표기 \"무결성\"을 써야 한다.",
  "cost-effectiveness: in selecting a monitoring methodology, the improvements from greater accuracy shall be balanced against additional costs. monitoring and reporting of emissions shall aim for the highest achievable accuracy, unless that is technically not feasible or incurs unreasonable costs": "말뭉치에서 \"비용 효율성\"이 우세하다.",
